{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"{\n  \"files\": [\n    {\n      \"content\": \"#include <bits/stdc++.h>\\n\\nusing namespace std;\\n\\nint A[1000][1000];\\nint ps[1010][1010];\\n\\ntypedef long long ll;\\n\\nll solve(int m, int n, int k) {\\n  const int d = min(m, n);\\n  const int length = max(m, n);\\n\\n  // Each prefix boundary stores a contiguous vector along the longer axis.\\n  fill(ps[0], ps[0] + length, 0);\\n  if (m <= n) {\\n    for (int b = 1; b <= d; b++) {\\n      const int* previous = ps[b - 1];\\n      const int* row = A[b - 1];\\n      int* current = ps[b];\\n      for (int i = 0; i < length; i++) {\\n        current[i] = previous[i] + row[i];\\n      }\\n    }\\n  } else {\\n    for (int b = 1; b <= d; b++) {\\n      const int* previous = ps[b - 1];\\n      int* current = ps[b];\\n      for (int i = 0; i < length; i++) {\\n        current[i] = previous[i] + A[i][b - 1];\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  unordered_map<ll, ll> h;\\n  ll ans = 0;\\n  for (int first = 0; first < d; first++) {\\n    const int* lower = ps[first];\\n    for (int last = first + 1; last <= d; last++) {\\n      const int* upper = ps[last];\\n      h.clear();\\n      h[0] = 1;\\n      ll s = 0;\\n      for (int i = 0; i < length; i++) {\\n        s += upper[i] - lower[i];\\n        ans += h.find(s - k) != h.end() ? h[s - k] : 0;\\n        h[s]++;\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n  return ans;\\n}\\n\\nint main() {\\n  ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\\n  cin.tie(nullptr);\\n\\n  int k, m, n;\\n  cin >> k >> m >> n;\\n\\n  for (int i = 0; i < m; i++)\\n    for (int j = 0; j < n; j++)\\n      cin >> A[i][j];\\n\\n  cout << solve(m, n, k) << endl;\\n  return 0;\\n}\\n\",\n      \"path\": \"src/main.cpp\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"hypothesis\": \"Pairing boundaries along the shorter dimension and scanning contiguous prefix vectors should improve locality and reduce enumeration work for wide matrices while preserving the reference frequency-counting kernel.\",\n  \"notes\": \"Unmeasured serial candidate; no commands executed. Every rectangle remains represented exactly once. Counts remain 64-bit, and boundary initialization supports repeated calls. The unchanged unordered_map kernel can be replaced independently.\",\n  \"research\": {\n    \"queries\": [],\n    \"urls\": []\n  },\n  \"sources_kept\": [],\n  \"transformations\": [\n    \"Enumerate boundary pairs along d=min(m,n), scanning L=max(m,n), for O(d²L) counting work.\",\n    \"Store prefix sums as boundary-major contiguous scan vectors and obtain band elements by subtracting two vectors.\",\n    \"Replace full-array clearing with explicit zero-boundary initialization on every solve call.\",\n    \"Disable iostream synchronization and untie cin without changing input or output bytes.\"\n  ]\n}"}}
